      "title": "Lecturer/Artist-in-Residence in Music Business and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Lecturer/Artist-in-Residence in Music Business and Entrepreneurship  - Winter Park, FL, Florida, United States Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Home Benefits Culture Location Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Lecturer/Artist-in-Residence in Music Business and Entrepreneurship Winter Park, FL, Florida Music Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) Opening on: Aug 14 2026 Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary: The Department of Music at Rollins College is seeking a dynamic musician and music industry professional to join our faculty as a full-time Lecturer/Artist-in-Residence in Music Business and Entrepreneurship. The successful candidate may teach undergraduate music major elective courses in areas such as commercial music, American popular music, music publishing, music business and marketing. The appointee will collaborate with the faculty in continuing to develop music business related courses. Additional responsibilities will include teaching general education courses to both music majors and non-majors, and may include applied lessons or ensembles based on candidate experience. The appointee will also be expected to serve on departmental and faculty committees and participate in faculty governance as appropriate. Rollins College is a comprehensive liberal arts college located just north of Orlando, FL, a diverse metropolitan community with a thriving economic and cultural scene. Nearby Orlando International Airport provides easy access to U.S. and international destinations. The college emphasizes innovative and quality teaching in small classes and ranks number one among 121 Southern master’s-level universities in the annual rankings of “America’s Best Colleges,” released by U.S. News & World Report. Please visit the college website at www.rollins.edu . Minimum Qualifications and Education: Master’s degree in music or equivalent professional experience. Experience in the following areas: marketing, artist management, music publishing and licensing, music in media, media composition, entrepreneurship, and copyright. Demonstrated record as an innovative classroom teacher. Preferred Qualifications: At least 2 years of college-level teaching. Terminal degree. Documented experience in research and publication. Demonstrated record of music performance Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants must apply online via the College's employment website and upload the following materials as follows: Letter of interest outlining the candidates qualifications for the responsibilities described above. Curriculum vita Statement of teaching philosophy that presents the candidate's commitment to the liberal arts and to student development Contact information for three references **Review of applications will begin immediately until position is filled. Priority review will be given to applications received before September 30, 2026 .** Inquiries can be directed to: Dr. Caitlin Mohr Search Chair cmohr@rollins.edu Benefits & Perks: Paid Holidays and College Closure Days Eligible for Medical, Prescription, Dental & Vision Insurances (within 30 days of hire) 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account ($125+/month) 100% Employer-Paid Short & Long Term Disability Insurance Domestic Partner Benefits 11.5% Employer Retirement Contributions Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Free On-Campus Parking Free Access to Campus Amenities (gyms, pools, library, sporting events and more) Free Full Tuition for Employees and their Families Pet Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Award-Winning Wellbeing Programs Plus More! Additional Perks: Rollins College is conveniently located on multiple Lynx Bus Routes (Winter Park/Rosemont-9 &  Winter Park/Springs Village-23) and within walking distance from the Winter Park SunRail Station Local & National Discount Programs, including Winter Park Locations (i.e. shops, restaurants, gift cards, and more) Free E-Training Courses & Professional Development Opportunities IT Software & Laptop Discounts (Apple, Lenovo, and more) College Bookstore Discounts Annual Service Awards & Recognition Programs Discover what it's like to live in Orlando: Live, Work, Play and Learn Plus More! Click here to review our full benefits package! Equal Employment Opportunity: Rollins College is an equal opportunity institution. Rollins does not discriminate on the basis of sex, disability, race, age, religion, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical characteristics, or any other category protected by College policy or federal, state, or local law for employment and in our educational programs and activities. To learn more about our commitments, visit click here . Any applicant who requires reasonable accommodations for any part of the application or hiring process may contact us by phone or in writing to humanresources@rollins.edu | 407.646.2102. Employment Eligibility: All new employees must be eligible and show employment eligibility verification by the first date of employment at Rollins College, as legally required (e.g., Form I-9). Rollins College will require proof of authorization to work in the United States. Further, based on the September 18, 2026, Presidential Proclamation and separate executive order, the College may not be able to offer H-1B sponsorship. Particularly the College is not able to pay the required fee accompanying new H-1B visa petitions. FLSA Status: Exempt Service Months: 9 Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! First Name (required) 5eb69d0a Last Name (required) b2311951 Email (required) c8c96259 Job Alert e16e39ea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Liberal Arts College of Liberal Arts Employment Type Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Why Join Rollins? At Rollins College, we believe people thrive when they feel supported. Join a community that values flexibility, wellness, inclusion, and recognition. When our employees thrive, so do our students and our campus community! Total Rewards Rollins offers a variety of benefits for full-time and part-time roles: Generous Paid Time Off & Holidays Medical, Dental, Vision Insurances Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Employer Retirement Contributions Free Tuition for Employees & Families Domestic Partner Benefits Employee Assistance Program Pet Insurance Click here to learn more! Thriving Together Inclusive, mission-driven campus culture . Service Excellence : Delivering the Rollins experience is a shared responsibility Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) Chart Your Journey Here at Rollins. Minutes from Orlando, Steps Away From Endless Opportunities Located in Winter Park, Florida, (and just minutes away from Orlando), Rollins is perfectly positioned at the center of theme park adventures, thriving tech companies, and one of the nation’s most thriving job markets. Take a walk to award-winning dining on Park Ave. Hop on a 15-minute train ride to downtown Orlando’s growing arts scene and pro sports. Or sink your toes into the sand of one of the world's best beaches. Discover #ThisisOrlando! Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4b4b1e16 Last Name (required) 1178ac37 Email (required) d233d255 Refer someone to this job Appl