      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Accounting",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Accounting - Winter Park, FL, Florida, United States Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Home Benefits Culture Location Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Visiting Assistant Professor, Accounting Winter Park, FL, Florida Business Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) Opening on: Oct 15 2026 Academic Affairs Position Summary: The Department of Business at Rollins College is seeking applicants for a Visiting Assistant Professor in Accounting position for the Spring 2027 semester. The position includes teaching undergraduate accounting courses (e.g., Financial Accounting, Managerial Accounting) for business majors in the Department of Business. The course load is four (4) courses per semester. The undergraduate business programs at Rollins College are accredited by AACSB. The Department of Business offers undergraduate majors in Business Management and International Business. The Business Management major is offered to both Day and Evening Students. The normal teaching load is eight courses per academic year (four courses per semester). Rollins College is committed to liberal education and expects all faculty to contribute to the general education programs of the college. Summer teaching is available through the evening program. Rollins College is a comprehensive liberal arts college located just north of Orlando, FL, a diverse metropolitan community with a thriving economic and cultural scene. Nearby Orlando International Airport provides easy access to U.S. and international destinations. The college emphasizes innovative and quality teaching in small classes and ranks number one among 121 Southern master’s-level universities in the annual rankings of “America’s Best Colleges,” released by U.S. News & World Report. Please visit the college website at www.rollins.edu . Minimum Qualifications and Education: Master’s degree in business or accountancy Ability to develop and deliver curriculum Prior college-level teaching experience Preferred Qualifications: Degree from an AACSB accredited institution CPA credential Relevant professional accounting experience Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants must apply online via the College's employment website and upload the following materials as follows: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching excellence including a statement of teaching philosophy and sample course evaluations Provide three reference names and email addresses **Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until postion is closed.** Please direct any questions to: Dr. David Caban Chair, Search Committee DCABAN@Rollins.edu Equal Employment Opportunity: Rollins College is an equal opportunity institution. Rollins does not discriminate on the basis of sex, disability, race, age, religion, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical characteristics, or any other category protected by College policy or federal, state, or local law for employment and in our educational programs and activities. To learn more about our commitments, click here . Any applicant who requires reasonable accommodations for any part of the application or hiring process may contact us by phone or in writing to humanresources@rollins.edu | 407.646.2102. Employment Eligibility: All new employees must be eligible and show employment eligibility verification by the first date of employment at Rollins College, as legally required (e.g., Form I-9). Rollins College will require proof of authorization to work in the United States. Further, based on the September 18, 2026, Presidential Proclamation and separate executive order, the College may not be able to offer H-1B sponsorship. Particularly the College is not able to pay the required fee accompanying new H-1B visa petitions. FLSA Status: Exempt Service Months: 5 Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! First Name (required) 130bde8d Last Name (required) 4514fca4 Email (required) 4a0a87ae Job Alert 74c15f65 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Liberal Arts College of Liberal Arts Employment Type Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Why Join Rollins? At Rollins College, we believe people thrive when they feel supported. Join a community that values flexibility, wellness, inclusion, and recognition. When our employees thrive, so do our students and our campus community! Total Rewards Rollins offers a variety of benefits for full-time and part-time roles: Generous Paid Time Off & Holidays Medical, Dental, Vision Insurances Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Employer Retirement Contributions Free Tuition for Employees & Families Domestic Partner Benefits Employee Assistance Program Pet Insurance Click here to learn more! Thriving Together Inclusive, mission-driven campus culture . Service Excellence : Delivering the Rollins experience is a shared responsibility Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) Chart Your Journey Here at Rollins. Minutes from Orlando, Steps Away From Endless Opportunities Located in Winter Park, Florida, (and just minutes away from Orlando), Rollins is perfectly positioned at the center of theme park adventures, thriving tech companies, and one of the nation’s most thriving job markets. Take a walk to award-winning dining on Park Ave. Hop on a 15-minute train ride to downtown Orlando’s growing arts scene and pro sports. Or sink your toes into the sand of one of the world's best beaches. Discover #ThisisOrlando! Ready to Apply? First Name (required) ae8cb8b7 Last Name (required) c6cf5c48 Email (required) 5179358d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1000 Holt Ave. Winter Park, FL 32789 Phone: 407.646.2000 Campus Map & Directions ADMISSION INFORMATION Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Graduate Business and Executive Education Professional Advancement Graduate Studies INFORMATION FOR Faculty & Staff Current Students Alumni & Supporters Parents & Families RESOURCES Library MyRollins Registrar Campus Map Events Calendar Rollins News Emergency Info INFORMATION ABOUT Rollins Sports Giving Arts & Culture Rollins Careers Bookstore For the Media EASE Grant Performance Measures Privacy Policy | Terms and Conditions | Accessibility Statement | Title IX Policies & Resources | Nondiscrimination Policy © 2026 Rollins College Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s) Opens in new window PDF Download Word Download Excel Download PowerPoint Download Document Download Explore your accessibility options"
