    "https://jobs.rollins.edu/jobs/associate-full-professor-entrepreneurship-orlando-florida-united-states-winter-park-fl": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor – Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor – Entrepreneurship - Winter Park, FL, Florida, United States Home Benefits Culture Location Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Associate/Full Professor – Entrepreneurship Winter Park, FL, Florida Crummer Graduate School of Business Faculty (Tenure-Track) Opening on: Oct 20 2026 Academic Affairs Position Summary: The Crummer Graduate School of Business at Rollins College invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Associate or Full Professor in Entrepreneurship beginning in Fall 2027. We seek an accomplished teacher-scholar who understands entrepreneurship as the creation, growth, and renewal of business. Our interests extend beyond new venture formation to include accelerating the growth of small and midsize enterprises, scaling established businesses, entrepreneurship through acquisition, and developing new opportunities within existing organizations. We are particularly interested in candidates who can connect rigorous academic thinking with the practical challenges of growing revenues, improving profitability, building organizational capabilities, and sustaining competitive advantage. The Crummer School teaches MBA students only, and we only hire experienced faculty, many of whom have won teaching awards and have demonstrated connections to industry practice prior to joining Crummer. The successful candidate will enjoy teaching MBAs, aspire to expand and develop top-tier graduate teaching skills, and demonstrate a strong commitment to best practices in teaching MBA students in-person and in blended formats that incorporate online learning. Teaching will focus primarily on graduate courses in entrepreneurship across Crummer’s four MBA programs: Early Advantage MBA (EAMBA – full-time students), Accelerated MBA (AMBA – full-time students with a STEM focus), Professional MBA (evening part-time students), and Executive MBA (primarily weekend students with substantial prior experience). We offer students the opportunity to gain an Entrepreneurship Concentration, and we also offer a Graduate Certificate in Entrepreneurship. Given the array of different programs mentioned above, our student body at Crummer includes varying ages and levels of experience, ranging from recent college graduates to senior executives. Our students rightfully expect much of us, and we encourage them to challenge and stimulate us as much as we do them. A defining feature of entrepreneurship at Crummer is our engagement with the Central Florida business community. We view entrepreneurship as a driver of business formation, expansion, and regional economic development. Our faculty and students engage with entrepreneurs, business owners, family enterprises, growth-oriented small and midsize companies, and established organizations pursuing new opportunities. Through applied projects, consulting, mentoring, and executive education, we seek to help businesses address real challenges in strategy, marketing, finance, operations, technology adoption, and organizational growth. For this position, we are particularly interested in someone who can successfully guide students toward a deep understanding of both the analytical processes that go into entrepreneurial businesses and the judgment required to frame meaningful business problems, evaluate data and analytical outputs, recognize limitations and uncertainties, and translate the analyses into sound managerial decisions and strategy-making. The Crummer School places high value on faculty who can work effectively with organizations, managers, and executives. The willingness and ability to consult with companies, understand real business problems and opportunities, and design and deliver high-quality executive education is important. Our entrepreneurship faculty engage with business owners, entrepreneurs, executives, investors, and professional advisers across businesses at different stages of development. These relationships create opportunities for student consulting projects, business growth initiatives, mentorship, executive education, and applied learning that addresses real organizational challenges. The Faculty Role at Crummer Crummer is a graduate business school in which teaching and student development are the largest part of the faculty role. Faculty responsibilities are approximately 50 percent teaching and student development, 30 percent scholarship, and 20 percent service and institutional stewardship. The standard teaching load is 15 credits per year. At Crummer, teaching means more than in-classroom hours and course delivery. We expect faculty to know their students, understand their aspirations, advise and mentor them, and help them connect what they learn directly to their professional development. Engagement with businesses is an important part of that work. Faculty who consult with companies, teach executives, and maintain strong relationships with managers and business leaders bring current problems, opportunities, and perspectives back into the classroom. These relationships frequently also create experiential learning opportunities, strengthen curriculum, and help students connect more effectively to the world of practice. We seek a colleague who combines academic strength with genuine expert engagement in entrepreneurship. Thus, the successful candidate will be someone who wants to work closely with students, remain connected to business theory and practice, engage credibly with managers and executives, collaborate with colleagues, and take shared responsibility for the quality and reputation of the School. In addition, of course scholarship remains an important part of the role. Faculty are expected to maintain an active research agenda and a record of peer-reviewed scholarship consistent with Crummer’s faculty bylaws and AACSB expectations for a graduate school of business. In terms of faculty service, key elements include faculty governance, curriculum and program development, admissions and recruitment, and other work that contributes to the effective operation and continued development of the School. As a relatively small graduate business school (we currently have 18 full-time faculty members), we value faculty who themselves fully embrace the worth of being a good institutional citizen and steward of Crummer and Rollins College. We do not have departments within the Crummer School and we highly value collaboration among faculty across the various business disciplines, as well as with our staff members. Within the Crummer culture, we are nimble and operate with little bureaucracy. The Opportunity The successful candidate for Full/Associate Professor of Entrepreneurship will step into an already active entrepreneurship program with a long and successful history at Crummer. The new colleague will also have the opportunity to help shape how Crummer teaches entrepreneurship and innovation in today’s rapidly changing environment, develop new courses and learning experiences, work across disciplines, engage with companies, contribute to executive education, and build connections with Central Florida’s incredibly vibrant business community. They will be supported by faculty colleagues teaching related topics such as design thinking, data analytics, and all of the traditional functional areas of business. About Crummer and Rollins The Crummer Graduate School of Business is an AACSB-accredited graduate business school at Rollins College. Crummer’s MBA is ranked No. 1 in Florida on LinkedIn’s 2026 list of Top 100 Global MBA Programs and has been recognized among the world’s top 100 MBA programs for three consecutive years. Crummer also offers a graduate-focused environment with a relatively small faculty, close engagement with students, and opportunities to contribute meaningfully to curriculum, programs, and the direction of the School. Rollins College brings a strong liberal arts tradition to graduate business education. It emphasizes critical thinking, communication, ethical reasoning, and understanding human and organizational context. Within this environment, Crummer is building its capacity in data analytics and AI, as these fields are playing a greater role in managerial decision-making, as well as supporting new and existing entrepreneurial ventures. Minimum Qualifications and Education: Ph.D. or Doctorate of Business Administration in Entrepreneurship, Management, or a closely related field from an AACSB or equivalently accredited institution. At least four years of full-time teaching experience at the rank of assistant professor or higher at an AACSB or equivalently accredited institution. Demonstrated teaching excellence in entrepreneurship and/or closely-related classes. Strong grounding in the concepts, methodologies, and applications of entrepreneurship research, practice, and teaching. Demonstrated record of peer-reviewed scholarship and an active research agenda consistent with Crummer and AACSB expectations. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching entrepreneurship in MBA or other graduate business programs in traditional in-person, blended, and online environments. Demonstrated ability to connect entrepreneurship education with building and enhancing successful entrepreneurial ventures. Experience consulting with companies. Professional or industry experience that strengthens the candidate’s ability to connect academic ideas with business practice. Experience working with organizations and practitioners in ways that strengthen teaching, student development, or applied learning. Record of constructive institutional engagement and collaboration. Evidence of meaningful engagement with students beyond the classroom. High-impact ways to foster such engagement include, but are not limited to: Working with small and midsize businesses on revenue growth, profitability, market expansion, and organizational challenges. Advising business owners and entrepreneurs on growth strategy, business models, succession, and acquisition opportunities. Developing experiential projects in which MBA students help existing businesses solve meaningful problems. Connecting students with entrepreneurs, business owners, executives, investors, and regional business organizations. Supporting graduates who launch, acquire, manage, or grow businesses throughout their careers. Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants must apply online via the College's employment website and upload the following materials as follows: Letter of interest Curriculum vita Evidence of sustained teaching excellence, particularly in graduate or professional education Contact information for three references on application **Review of applications will begin immediately until the position is closed. Preference will be given to applications received by November 15, 2026.** Inquiries can be directed to: Dr. Greg Marshall Charles Harwood Professor of Marketing and Strategy Chair, Entrepreneurship Faculty Search Committee gmarshall@rollins.edu Benefits & Perks: Paid Holidays and College Closure Days Eligible for Medical, Prescription, Dental & Vision Insurances (within 30 days of hire) 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account ($125+/month) 100% Employer-Paid Short & Long Term Disability Insurance Domestic Partner Benefits 11.5% Employer Retirement Contributions Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Free On-Campus Parking Free Access to Campus Amenities (gyms, pools, library, sporting events and more) Free Full Tuition for Employees and their Families Pet Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Award-Winning Wellbeing Programs Plus More! Additional Perks: Rollins College is conveniently located on multiple Lynx Bus Routes (Winter Park/Rosemont-9 &  Winter Park/Springs Village-23) and within walking distance from the Winter Park SunRail Station Local & National Discount Programs, including Winter Park Locations (i.e. shops, restaurants, gift cards, and more) Free E-Training Courses & Professional Development Opportunities IT Software & Laptop Discounts (Apple, Lenovo, and more) College Bookstore Discounts Annual Service Awards & Recognition Programs Discover what it's like to live in Orlando: Live, Work, Play and Learn Plus More! Click here to review our full benefits package! Equal Employment Opportunity: Rollins College is an equal opportunity institution. Rollins does not discriminate on the basis of sex, disability, race, age, religion, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical characteristics, or any other category protected by College policy or federal, state, or local law for employment and in our educational programs and activities. To learn more about our commitments, visit click here . Any applicant who requires reasonable accommodations for any part of the application or hiring process may contact us by phone or in writing to humanresources@rollins.edu | 407.646.2102. Employment Eligibility: All new employees must be eligible and show employment eligibility verification by the first date of employment at Rollins College, as legally required (e.g., Form I-9). Rollins College will require proof of authorization to work in the United States. Further, based on the September 18, 2026, Presidential Proclamation and separate executive order, the College may not be able to offer H-1B sponsorship. Particularly the College is not able to pay the required fee accompanying new H-1B visa petitions. FLSA Status: Exempt Service Months: 9 Apply now! Why Join Rollins? At Rollins College, we believe people thrive when they feel supported. Join a community that values flexibility, wellness, inclusion, and recognition. When our employees thrive, so do our students and our campus community! Total Rewards Rollins offers a variety of benefits for full-time and part-time roles: Generous Paid Time Off & Holidays Medical, Dental, Vision Insurances Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Employer Retirement Contributions Free Tuition for Employees & Families Domestic Partner Benefits Employee Assistance Program Pet Insurance Click here to learn more! Thriving Together Inclusive, mission-driven campus culture . Service Excellence : Delivering the Rollins experience is a shared responsibility Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) Chart Your Journey Here at Rollins. Minutes from Orlando, Steps Away From Endless Opportunities Located in Winter Park, Florida, (and just minutes away from Orlando), Rollins is perfectly positioned at the center of theme park adventures, thriving tech companies, and one of the nation’s most thriving job markets. Take a walk to award-winning dining on Park Ave. Hop on a 15-minute train ride to downtown Orlando’s growing arts scene and pro sports. Or sink your toes into the sand of one of the world's best beaches. Discover #ThisisOrlando! 1000 Holt Ave. Winter Park, FL 32789 Phone: 407.646.2000 Campus Map & Directions ADMISSION INFORMATION Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Graduate Business and Executive Education Professional Advancement Graduate Studies INFORMATION FOR Faculty & Staff Current Students Alumni & Supporters Parents & Families RESOURCES Library MyRollins Registrar Campus Map Events Calendar Rollins News Emergency Info INFORMATION ABOUT Rollins Sports Giving Arts & Culture Rollins Careers Bookstore For the Media EASE Grant Performance Measures Privacy Policy | Terms and Conditions | Accessibility Statement | Title IX Policies & Resources | Nondiscrimination Policy © 2026 Rollins College Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
